Subject: [PATCH 0003] Do not bind() the limited-broadcast address on Darwin

DeviceManager::CreateDetectionChannel() and CreateCommandChannel() create an
extra UDP socket bound to the literal address 255.255.255.255. Linux permits
this; macOS/Darwin returns EADDRNOTAVAIL, util::CreateSocket() returns -1, and
DeviceManager::Init() therefore fails outright:

    bind failed
    [error] Create detection broadcast socket failed.  [device_manager.cpp:266]
    [error] Create detection channel failed.           [device_manager.cpp:242]
    [error] Create channel failed.                     [device_manager.cpp:169]
    Livox Init Failed

i.e. *unpatched Livox-SDK2 cannot start on macOS at all*, with or without real
hardware. Both call sites are already wrapped in `#ifdef WIN32 / #else`, so the
minimal fix is to treat Darwin like Win32. The broadcast-bound sockets are only
an additional receive path for detection ACKs and pushed state; the sockets
bound to the configured host IP still receive both by unicast, which is how a
Mid-360 configured with an explicit host_ip actually talks.

Consequence for A3: on macOS, zero-configuration "view mode" discovery of a
lidar whose IP is not yet known will not work. A3 must require an explicit
lidar IP in the config on macOS (which the LidarScan connect wizard does
anyway, per spec 3.1).
---
--- a/sdk_core/device_manager.cpp
+++ b/sdk_core/device_manager.cpp
@@ -259,7 +259,11 @@
 }
 
 bool DeviceManager::CreateDetectionChannel() {
-#ifdef WIN32
+#if defined(WIN32) || defined(__APPLE__)
+  // macOS (Darwin) refuses bind(2) to the limited-broadcast address 255.255.255.255
+  // with EADDRNOTAVAIL, unlike Linux. The extra broadcast-bound socket is only an
+  // additional receive path for detection ACKs; the host-IP-bound detection socket
+  // created below already receives unicast ACKs. Skip it here, as WIN32 already does.
 #else
   detection_broadcast_socket_ = util::CreateSocket(kDetectionPort, true, true, true, "255.255.255.255", "");
   if (detection_broadcast_socket_ < 0) {
@@ -324,7 +328,8 @@
     }
   }
 
-#ifdef WIN32
+#if defined(WIN32) || defined(__APPLE__)
+  // See CreateDetectionChannel(): Darwin cannot bind 255.255.255.255.
 #else
   if (dev_type == kLivoxLidarTypeMid360 || dev_type == kLivoxLidarTypeMid360s || dev_type == kLivoxLidarTypeAvia2) {
     socket_t broadcast_socket = util::CreateSocket(host_net_info.push_msg_port, true, true, true, "255.255.255.255", "");
